  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Wakix (pitolisant) Criteria Version 1; Original 3/11/2021; Approval 4/16/2021; Effective 2021-05-24. Approval criteria and explicit denials encoded; diagnostic and therapy documentation attestations require manual review.",
    "Denial criterion 4 contains awkward wording (\"Patient is not and will no use drugs that prolong the QT interval\"). Interpreted as denial for using QT-prolonging drugs, consistent with source intent; no management exception is encoded.",
    "Cautions (notes only): WAKIX may reduce effectiveness of sensitive CYP3A4 substrates, including hormonal contraceptives. Use alternative non-hormonal contraception during treatment and for at least 21 days after discontinuation. With strong CYP2D6 inhibitors, maximum recommended dosage is 17.8 mg once daily.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 6 months with clinically meaningful chart notes showing positive response to therapy. Manual review required.",
    "Quantity limits (notes only): 53 \u00d7 8.9 mg tablets per 30 days; 60 \u00d7 17.8 mg tablets per 30 days. Quantity enforcement requires manual review."
  ],
